{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3255","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3255","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3255\",\"parent_revision\":\"d1a233f5ccce1c41b20d18d0c0c9c1b506e62270bbce813a117a13966e8df065\",\"root_revision\":\"d1a233f5ccce1c41b20d18d0c0c9c1b506e62270bbce813a117a13966e8df065\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-27\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nGoal: every `stage_skills` entry in `plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3/language-manifest.yaml` and `plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3-cli/language-manifest.yaml` should resolve to something loadable, since `plugins/development-harness/agents/generic-stage-agent.md` and `plugins/development-harness/scripts/dispatch_helper.py` load every `stage_skills` value via `Skill(skill=\\\"...\\\")`.\\n\\nObservations (verified this session while fixing #3254):\\n- Neither `plugins/python3-development/skills/` nor `plugins/python3-development/agents/` contains anything named `python3-discovery`, `python3-implementation`, `python3-implementation-cli`, `python3-planning-task-decomposition`, `python3-testing-forensic-review`, or `python3-testing` \u2014 every one of these is a broken `Skill()` load target.\\n- `python3/language-manifest.yaml` stage_skills: `discovery: [python3-discovery]`, `planning-context-integration: [python3-implementation]`, `planning-task-decomposition: [python3-planning-task-decomposition]`, `implementation: [python3-implementation]`, `testing-forensic-review: [python3-testing-forensic-review]`, `testing-final-verification: [python3-testing]` \u2014 all six are unresolvable skill names.\\n- `python3-cli/language-manifest.yaml` stage_skills: `implementation: [python3-implementation-cli]` \u2014 also unresolvable.\\n- The `design` field in both files was already fixed under #3254/P28cf6743/T1 to `python3-development:python-cli-design-spec` (an agent, loaded via `profile_load`, per the special-cased Phase 3 design-spec role resolution in `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md`). That fix does not cover the other stage_skills fields above, which use the generic `Skill()`-load path instead of `profile_load`.\\n- Test fixtures (`plugins/development-harness/tests/test_manifest_resolver.py`, `test_manifest_schema.py`, `test_dispatch_helper.py`, `test_manifest_merge.py`, `test_proof_of_concept.py`) use these same placeholder names as inline YAML strings, not by reading the real manifest files, so they pass regardless of whether the real manifest names resolve to anything.\\n\\nImpact: any SAM stage dispatch through `generic-stage-agent` for the python3/python3-cli manifests (discovery, planning-context-integration, planning-task-decomposition, implementation, testing-forensic-review, testing-final-verification stages) attempts to load a skill that does not exist. Per `add-new-feature/SKILL.md`'s Domain Signal Detection step, a failed skill load logs a warning and continues rather than hard-failing, so this may be silently degrading dispatch quality rather than causing visible errors \u2014 worth confirming during grooming.\\n\\nUser-provided context: possible fix is either (a) create the missing skills under `plugins/python3-development/skills/` with those names, or (b) repoint each `stage_skills` entry at an existing skill (e.g. `python3-development:python3-add-feature`, `python3-development:python3-test-design`) \u2014 needs a design decision on which skills should own each SDLC stage, not a mechanical rename like #3254's design fix.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Discovered while fixing #3254 (stage_skills.design \u2192 python-cli-design-spec)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-27\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"54a0531a5a45a28bd667f4ae1335b5723fefc5f8f0543c5b21b5e3613264d098\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRBat8A\"}"}